{
  "name": "Shri Tools Connect - make a video",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Shri Tools Connect\n1. Start **Shri Tools** (desktop shortcut). In Shri Tools > **Connect** you can set an API key (optional on this laptop) and download this workflow with your key already filled in.\n2. Edit **Your video** (title, idea, season, language) and click **Test workflow**, or call the webhook **POST /webhook/shritub-connect** with the same fields as JSON.\n3. Shri Tools writes the story, draws the pictures, makes every scene with MiniMax H3 (voices + sounds), checks them, joins the final video and makes a Short, thumbnails and YouTube texts. This flow checks every 10 minutes (one scene takes ~10 min on a 4 GB GPU, an 18-scene episode ~4 h).\n4. **Download final video** gives the mp4 as binary: connect **YouTube > Upload** after it. Titles, description and tags are in `video.publish` of the last check.\n\nFields: title, idea (or scenes), season (title) or season_id, language (en, hi, kn, kok, mr, ta, te, ml, bn, gu, pa, ur), style (pixar, cinematic, anime, storybook, clay), cast (names), scenes_wanted, approve_pictures (true = stop after the pictures until you press Make videos), callback_url.",
        "height": 540,
        "width": 580
      },
      "id": "7b1c0e10-2a3d-4e5f-9a00-000000000001",
      "name": "How to use",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -260,
        -640
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "7b1c0e10-2a3d-4e5f-9a00-000000000002",
      "name": "Start (manual)",
